WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.704
Why can a six-variable table contain a function that really depends on only three variables?

q0002
00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:16.767
This episode has one job: The surrounding assignment universe may name more variables than the function can actually depend on after simplification or fixed bindings.

q0003
00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:25.830
We build on Expression, truth table, and Boolean function; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:34.501
Live support contains variables that can change the output; ambient variables merely belong to the surrounding layout.

q0005
00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:42.205
Watch for the label live support; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:42.205 --> 00:00:49.426
When we say ambient variable, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:49.426 --> 00:00:58.097
The term fixed binding receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:00:58.097 --> 00:01:06.768
The next sequence uses Four-variable truth layout as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0009
00:01:06.768 --> 00:01:10.605
Our stable example is Four-variable truth layout.

q0010
00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:19.668
F(A,B,C,D)=(A AND B) XOR (C OR D), row variables A,B, column variables C,D, MSB-first ordering.

q0011
00:01:19.668 --> 00:01:26.889
Carry assignments, live support, explicit CM, packed truth vectors, and exact output across episodes.

q0012
00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:34.110
We now construct the Four-variable truth layout and name every part before interpreting it.

q0013
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:41.331
Hold one input fixed and test which remaining variables can still change the output.

q0014
00:01:41.331 --> 00:01:49.035
Collapse duplicate ambient rows into the smaller semantic-support view without claiming an automatic timing gain.

q0015
00:01:49.035 --> 00:01:53.355
Now isolate live support inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0016
00:01:53.355 --> 00:02:01.542
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for live support changes.

q0017
00:02:01.542 --> 00:02:09.729
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to live support, not to a substituted workload.

q0018
00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:15.499
Nominal width and live support settle as two separate labeled counters.

q0019
00:02:15.499 --> 00:02:19.819
Now isolate ambient universe inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0020
00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:28.006
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for ambient universe changes.

q0021
00:02:28.006 --> 00:02:36.193
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to ambient universe, not to a substituted workload.

q0022
00:02:36.193 --> 00:02:41.963
Ambient variables form an outer ring; only output-changing wires remain bright.

q0023
00:02:41.963 --> 00:02:46.283
Now isolate fixed-variable reduction inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0024
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:54.470
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for fixed-variable reduction changes.

q0025
00:02:54.470 --> 00:03:02.657
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to fixed-variable reduction, not to a substituted workload.

q0026
00:03:02.657 --> 00:03:09.394
A fixed binding removes one axis while paired rows collapse onto identical outputs.

q0027
00:03:09.394 --> 00:03:18.457
Live support and ambient variables are distinct: live variables affect the function, while ambient variables may still define the displayed assignment universe.

q0028
00:03:18.457 --> 00:03:24.227
Read that statement only within this scope: CM IR materialization semantics.

q0029
00:03:24.227 --> 00:03:27.580
Its declared measurement boundary is representation.

q0030
00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.450
The uncertainty field says none.

q0031
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:39.513
The nearest confusing lesson is What a correspondence matrix is; it owns row/column variable partition, while this episode owns live support.

q0032
00:03:39.513 --> 00:03:48.576
The example fixes F of A, B, C, and D as A AND B, exclusive-or C OR D.

q0033
00:03:48.576 --> 00:03:53.863
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate live support.

q0034
00:03:53.863 --> 00:04:02.926
A and B select the row, C and D select the column, and MSB-first order fixes both index conventions.

q0035
00:04:02.926 --> 00:04:08.213
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate ambient universe.

q0036
00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:17.276
Every four-bit assignment names exactly one of the sixteen cells, and every cell returns one exact output bit.

q0037
00:04:17.276 --> 00:04:22.563
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate fixed-variable reduction.

q0038
00:04:22.563 --> 00:04:30.267
Folding the truth-table output column into a four-by-four grid changes the layout, not the function.

q0039
00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:39.330
Reading a cell forward evaluates an assignment; reading it backward recovers the row and column bits that selected it.

q0040
00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:48.393
Live support can remove an input from active computation even when the ambient layout still reserves its axis.

q0041
00:04:48.393 --> 00:04:57.456
A packed truth vector stores the same exact outputs in a different physical arrangement from the displayed matrix.

q0042
00:04:57.456 --> 00:05:06.519
The explicit matrix is dense by contract, so compactness and speed require separate evidence rather than definition alone.

q0043
00:05:06.519 --> 00:05:15.582
Smaller live support changes the active problem description, but it does not by itself select the fastest engine.

q0044
00:05:15.582 --> 00:05:24.253
Identify which variable is ambient after two assignments produce the same output under both of its values.

q0045
00:05:24.253 --> 00:05:28.573
Nominal width and semantic support answer different questions.

q0046
00:05:28.573 --> 00:05:36.277
A common mistake is this: Every named variable necessarily doubles the function's active computational support.

q0047
00:05:36.277 --> 00:05:41.564
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: live support.

q0049
00:05:44.585 --> 00:05:52.289
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: Nominal width and semantic support answer different questions.

q0050
00:05:52.289 --> 00:05:59.993
Count the variables that matter to this function, not only the variables named around it.
